  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4971c5eb32d68c6419c2b82ec69e3fa3, type: 3}
  m_Name: DadStareTwo
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NarratorEventData
  eventID: DadStareTwo
  dialogueLines:
  - The player has been staring at their dad for a very long time. This is becoming
    uncomfortable.
  - The player is still watching their dad. The narrator is beginning to feel rather
    uneasy about this.
  - Dad has noticed the staring. Perhaps the player should look somewhere else.
  - "The player hasn\u2019t looked away once. This is starting to get a little unsettling."
  - The player continues to stare at Dad. The narrator is beginning to question their
    intentions.
  - "That\u2019s quite enough staring. Even the narrator is starting to feel uncomfortable."
  - "Dad is trying to work, but the player continues to watch. Perhaps that\u2019s
    enough."
  - The player has been staring for an uncomfortable amount of time. Maybe look away
    now.
  - Still staring. The narrator is starting to think this has gone beyond simple
    curiosity.
  - The player continues to watch their dad in silence. The narrator would really
    prefer they stopped.
  canRepeat: 1
